<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Coding Project Ideas</title>

    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #f3f7ff;
            padding: 30px;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: auto;
        }

        h1 {
            text-align: center;
            color: #315aa8;
        }

        .project {
            background: white;
            padding: 20px;
            margin: 15px 0;
            border-radius: 14px;
            box-shadow: 0 3px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.07);
        }

        .project h2 {
            color: #315aa8;
        }

        .level {
            display: inline-block;
            padding: 7px 12px;
            background: #e8efff;
            border-radius: 15px;
            font-size: 14px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

<div class="container">

    <h1>💡 Coding Project Ideas</h1>

    <div class="project">
        <h2>1. Student Marks Calculator</h2>
        <p>Create a program that calculates total and average marks.</p>
        <span class="level">Beginner</span>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
        <h2>2. Quiz Application</h2>
        <p>Create a simple application containing questions and answers.</p>
        <span class="level">Beginner</span>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
        <h2>3. Library Management System</h2>
        <p>Create a system to manage books and student borrowing records.</p>
        <span class="level">Intermediate</span>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
        <h2>4. Personal Portfolio</h2>
        <p>Create a website that introduces your skills, education and projects.</p>
        <span class="level">Beginner</span>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
        <h2>5. Expense Tracker</h2>
        <p>Create a project to record income and expenses.</p>
        <span class="level">Intermediate</span>
    </div>

</div>

</body>
</html>
